The crash is a stack-buffer-overflow READ 8. Let me look at the `SC_ASN1_BIT_FIELD` case in `asn1_decode_entry` more carefully. The `decode_bit_field` function reads `data[i/8]` where `data` is `u8 data[sizeof(unsigned int)]` = 4 bytes on 32-bit or 8 bytes on 64-bit. The loop `for (i = 0; i < n; i += 8)` reads `data[i/8]`. If `n` is larger than `sizeof(data)*8`, this would read out of bounds.

But wait, `decode_bit_string` checks `if (outlen < octets_left) return SC_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;` where `outlen = sizeof(data) = 8` (on 64-bit). So `octets_left` can be at most 8, meaning `n` can be at most `8*8 - zero_bits = 64`. The loop `for (i = 0; i < n; i += 8)` reads `data[i/8]` for `i = 0, 8, 16, ..., 56`, so `data[0]` through `data[7]` - that's fine for 8-byte data.

